---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { ENTITY } from "../data/legal";

const UPDATED = "2026-10-12";
---

<LegalLayout
	title="Terms of Use"
	description="The terms that apply to your use of the MedicSupport Network website."
	updated={UPDATED}
>
	<h2>About these terms</h2>
	<p>
		These terms apply to your use of the {ENTITY.tradingName} website. By using the site you
		accept them. If you do not accept them, please stop using the site.
	</p>
	<p>
		The company operating this site is <strong>{ENTITY.name}</strong>, registered in
		{ENTITY.registration}, with its registered office at {ENTITY.address}.
	</p>

	<h2>What this website is — and is not</h2>
	<p>
		We are a hospital and clinic group. We own and operate hospitals and clinics across
		Africa and Asia, and we employ our own clinicians. Some of those clinicians are
		seconded to hospitals in Europe and America.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>
			Nothing on this website is medical advice, a diagnosis, a treatment recommendation, or
			an offer of treatment.
		</strong>
		If you need care, contact a clinician or an emergency service. Do not rely on this site
		to decide whether to seek urgent medical attention.
	</p>

	<h2>Credential verification</h2>
	<p>
		We publish clinician profiles and reference numbers so that a professional body,
		employer or patient can confirm that a person is who they claim to be and holds the
		registration we have verified.
	</p>
	<p>
		<strong>
			A verification result confirms only what was checked, on what date, against which
			register.
		</strong> It is not a fitness-to-practise certificate, not a guarantee of current
		competence, and not an endorsement by us of a specific treatment. Registration status can
		change after the date shown on the record. Always confirm directly with the relevant
		register where a decision depends on it.
	</p>
	<p>
		We publish credential records we have verified and nothing else. Where a record is
		withdrawn, we remove it.
	</p>

	<h2>Intellectual property</h2>
	<p>
		The site design, text, logo and code are owned by {ENTITY.tradingName} or its licensors.
		You may view, print and share pages for your own use. You may not reproduce material to
		build a competing service, present our content as your own, or use our name or marks
		without written permission.
	</p>
	<p>
		Clinical and operational details about our facilities are ours to publish, but please do
		not scrape or republish them at scale.
	</p>

	<h2>Third-party links</h2>
	<p>
		Where we link to a professional register or another external body, we do not control it
		and are not responsible for its content or availability. A link is not an endorsement.
	</p>

	<h2>Enquiries and applications</h2>
	<p>
		Enquiries sent through this site are an invitation to discuss, not an offer, an
		engagement, or a contract. Any engagement is governed by a separate written agreement.
		Nothing on this site creates a contract between you and us.
	</p>

	<h2>Liability</h2>
	<p>
		To the extent permitted by law, we exclude liability for loss arising from reliance on
		the content of this site, and for any indirect or consequential loss. Nothing in these
		terms excludes liability for fraud, for death or personal injury caused by negligence,
		for clinical negligence, or for anything else that cannot lawfully be excluded.
	</p>
	<p>
		Nothing in these terms affects the statutory rights of patients treated at our facilities,
		which are governed by the law of the country where the treatment took place.
	</p>

	<h2>Availability</h2>
	<p>
		We aim to keep the site available but do not guarantee it. We may change, suspend or
		withdraw any part of it.
	</p>

	<h2>Governing law</h2>
	<p>
		These terms are governed by the law of {ENTITY.registration}, and the courts of that
		jurisdiction have exclusive jurisdiction, except that the mandatory rights of patients
		treat at our facilities remain governed by the law of the country where that treatment
		took place.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		<a href={`mailto:${ENTITY.generalEmail}`}>{ENTITY.generalEmail}</a>. Write to us at
		{ENTITY.address}.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>